# Keep the build context to the sources the image is built from.
#
# This file is load-bearing, not an optimisation. Without it `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile lands
# the *host's* node_modules on top of the Linux ones `npm ci` just installed — and better-sqlite3
# and isolated-vm are native modules, so a Windows or macOS host produces an image whose binaries
# cannot load. It also keeps the database, the dev encryption keys and the git history out of the
# build stage.

# Installed per-platform inside the image.
node_modules

# Runtime state: SQLite, proctoring snapshots, nightly backups, and the development
# APP_MASTER_KEY / SESSION_SECRET. None of it belongs in an image.
data

# Build outputs, produced inside the image by `npm run build`.
dist
dist-server
server/content
src/content/manifest.generated.ts
*.tsbuildinfo

# Fetched inside the image by scripts/fetch-mediapipe.mjs (~46 MB).
public/mediapipe

# Source assets that the image does not need.
Oyelearn-Logo-Kit
Oyelearn-Logo-Kit.zip

# Repository and editor metadata.
.git
.github
.gitignore
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local environment. The image reads configuration from the process environment.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Deployment and docs, not inputs to the build.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yml
Caddyfile.example
vercel.json
.vercelignore
docs
README.md
*.log
npm-debug.log*
